  {
   "id": "b2-25",
   "name": "Transformation of foodstuffs: notion and importance"
  }
 ],
 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Transformation (processing) of foodstuffs is changing raw farm products into new food products, for example cassava into garri, maize into flour, milk into yoghurt, cocoa into chocolate, groundnuts into oil.\nImportance and advantages:\n• food keeps longer and wastes less after harvest;\n• it is easier to store, carry and sell;\n• it makes new tastes and a varied diet;\n• some poisons are removed (soaking cassava removes cyanide);\n• it creates jobs and income.\nDisadvantages:\n• some vitamins and fibre can be lost (refined flour, polished rice);\n• too much salt, sugar or fat may be added;\n• poor hygiene can contaminate food;\n• machines and packaging cost money.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "f": "cassava"
  },
  "problem": "Give two reasons why {f} is processed into garri.",
  "steps": [
   "Fresh {f} rots within a few days, but dry garri keeps for months.",
   "Soaking and fermenting removes the poison (cyanide) in bitter {f}."
  ],
  "answer": "Garri keeps longer, and the poison is removed.",
  "checks": []
 },
